High-performing creators like @vaibhavsisinty frame technical topics around dramatic, high-value outcomes (e.g., "My 15,000 rupee TV now runs like a 1 lakh TV"). @garvit.irl starts videos with feature comparisons (e.g., "ChatGPT's Dots, Muse, and Grokbot..."), which targets technical viewers but misses the broader visual and problem-driven hook needed to drive viral reach.

3. Underutilization of Video Format Efficiency
@garvit.irl generates an average of 201 likes on Reels compared to just 31 likes on static posts. Competitors in the top tier rely 100% on short-form video reels that showcase tangible screen recordings, local code runs, or simulated environments rather than static carousels or image posts.


